ng a  personal attack against Elijah Cummings  he's making a professional attack the  man has had 36 years to clean up his own  district and it's only gotten worse  under his leadership so I think the the  attack against representative Cummings  is absolutely appropriate and of course  the the people of Baltimore which is  historically a wonderful city and has  fallen into very difficult times or they  deserve decent political leadership and  that has been deprived of them for the  past several decades but that's not  president Trump's fault president Trump  didn't cause the problems in Baltimore  and if he's shining a light on it now  then I hope that the people who are  actually responsible for that city will  respond but instead I think they want to  launch unfair attacks and malign the  character of the president rather than  actually clean up their own towns but  your colleague Ben Shapiro actually says  the president does not have a plan to  help Baltimore what do you make of that  well I'm a federalist as has been and as  are many other people so of course I  don't think the president has any  antipathy to where the people of  Baltimore I think  wants to help the people of Baltimore  but what at the federal level is the  President of the United States supposed  to do for a city that suffers from local  political corruption I'm very skeptical  of federal plans as Ronald Reagan used  to say the nine most dangerous words in  the English language or I'm from the  government and I'm here to help this  this is incumbent on people at the local  level and at the state level to do  something about it and I don't think we  need an answer for every single  political problem in the country from  the leader of the free world you had  suggested that that this might help the  president how is this gonna help the  president I mean this just seems to be  nasty politics people trading barbs on  on Twitter unfortunately though negative  politics works and unfortunately attack  ads work as well that's why all  politicians use them it would be  wonderful if the president were able to  make himself acceptable to a wide slew  of Americans and very kind and genial  and and operating in ways of individual  grace that we ourselves want to operate  in our political moment isn't terribly  graceful or charitable or merciful and  if he has attacks being lobbed against  him from Elijah Cummings and from all of  his other political opponents unfair  attacks maligning him he has to fight  back you know you have two different  tactical and strategic approaches you  have the kind genial Republicans Mitt  Romney say who want to stay away from  cultural issues and you have the culture  warriors who are not going to win so  much by making themselves acceptable but  by portraying their opponents as  unacceptable Governor Romney lost his  election for president President Trump  won his election and we'll see in 2020  if that strategy is going to to bear  fruit and in moving forward hey Michael  Knowles thank you so much from The Daily  wire appreciate your time perhaps  thank you very much
 

